WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.677
EXTRACT EPOCH returns the total number of seconds represented by an interval.

00:00:04.677 --> 00:00:08.592
From there, you can convert to hours or days.

00:00:08.592 --> 00:00:11.697
The unit you choose should match the analysis.

00:00:11.697 --> 00:00:16.017
A numeric duration is often convenient for statistics or modeling,

00:00:16.017 --> 00:00:20.832
while the interval type can be more expressive for SQL temporal operations.

00:00:20.832 --> 00:00:24.407
Date arithmetic should reflect the business definition.

00:00:24.407 --> 00:00:30.312
Calendar age, elapsed hours, and number of midnights are not always the same measure.

00:00:30.312 --> 00:00:36.892
In healthcare, length of stay may have an operational definition that differs from simple timestamp

00:00:36.892 --> 00:00:39.040
subtraction. Document the unit and the rule.
